%[text] # Size Data Center Cooling System
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] ## Setup System Model
%[text] ### Create Liquid Cooled Data Center
%[text] Create a 1 MW data center by parameterizing the **PDU + CDU Assembly (LUT)** composite library block. For more information about creating and parameterizing a data center block, see the [Create Liquid Cooled Data Center Model](file:../CreatePlantModels/CreateLiquidCooledDataCenterExample.m) example. Each PDU + CDU unit consists of three racks and six IT trays per rack. A 1 MW rating requires 36 such PDU + CDU assemblies. To verify this, click `Get Rating` on the block mask.
%[text] Specify start date and time for analysis.
modelData.StartDate = datetime(2025,1,1,1,0,0);
modelData.EndDate = datetime(2025,12,31,1,0,0);
modelData.DateTimeVec = modelData.StartDate:hours(1):modelData.EndDate;
%[text] Set desired temperature for PDU servers and the data center room.
modelData.ControlParam.Tset.PDU  = simscape.Value(300,"K");
modelData.ControlParam.Tset.ROOM = simscape.Value(283,"K");
%[text] ### Create Room Around Data Center
%[text] The data center room is modeled as a large rectangular room, with all PDU units dissipating heat to the air inside the room. The room physics is defined in the **Data Center in Building/Data Center Room** subsystem. The room is cooled by a heat exchanger, represented in the current model by the **HVAC (Room)** block.
%[text] ![](text:image:9656)
%[text] In the **Data Center in Building/Data Center Room** subsystem, the room is defined as a rectangular space with four walls, each containing a glass window. The glass window area on each wall is specified by the `Fraction wall area occupied by window (-)` parameter on the **Data Center Room** block mask. This parameter takes values between 0 and 1, where 0 indicates a completely solid wall with no glass window, and 1 indicates a wall made entirely of glass. The glass area coverage and the wall orientation, specified by the `Room orientation wrt South (deg)` parameter, determine the solar radiation that reaches the data center room. The Fraction room volume occupied by `Data Center units (-)` parameter specifies the volume of the room occupied by the data center assets, the PDU and the CDU. The default room orientation faces south (see the directions on the 2D plane shown above), and the entire room can be rotated using the `Room orientation wrt South (deg)` parameter on the **Data Center Room** block mask.
%[text] Specify data center room size and orientation.
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Length = simscape.Value(100,"m");
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Width  = simscape.Value(40,"m");
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Height = simscape.Value(5,"m");
modelData.ControlParam.Room.OrientationAngle = simscape.Value(30,"deg");
%[text] Specify room wall, roof, floor, and glass thickness.
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Thickness.Wall = simscape.Value(0.1,"m");
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Thickness.Glass = simscape.Value(5e-3,"m");
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Thickness.Floor = simscape.Value(0.11,"m");
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Thickness.Roof = simscape.Value(0.08,"m");
%[text] Specify glass transmissivity. This parameter (along with `Room.OrientationAngle` parameter) deterines the solar load reaching inside the room directly.
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Transmissivity.Glass = 0.45;
%[text] Specify the percentage coverage area of glass on the four walls.
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Wall1FracWindow = 0.75;
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Wall2FracWindow = 0.01;
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Wall3FracWindow = 0.75;
modelData.ControlParam.Room.Wall4FracWindow = 0.01;
%[text] Specify the fraction of room volume occupied by the data center.
modelData.ControlParam.Room.RoomVolFracAsset = 0.8;
%[text] To learn more above how to define rooms for buildings, see project [Building Energy Management System with Simscape](https://in.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/175604-building-energy-management-system-with-simscape).
%[text] ### Model Chiller, Cooling Tower, and Room HVAC
%[text] Chiller removes all heat transferred by the CDU unit in data center. Work done by chiller compressor is specified as: 
%[text]  $W=\\frac{Q\_{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{D}\\mathrm{U}} }{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{O}\\mathrm{P}}${"editStyle":"visual"}
%[text] Heat rejected at cooling tower is given by:
%[text]  $Q\_{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{T}} =Q\_{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{D}\\mathrm{U}} +W=Q\_{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{D}\\mathrm{U}} \\times \\left(1+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{O}\\mathrm{P}}\\right)${"editStyle":"visual"}
%[text] Cooling tower fan power consumption is given by:
%[text]  $P\_{\\mathrm{Fan}} =\\varepsilon\_{\\mathrm{CT}} \\times Q\_{\\mathrm{CT}}${"editStyle":"visual"}, where $\\varepsilon\_{\\mathrm{CT}}${"editStyle":"visual"} is the cooling tower fan power ratio (typically between 0.01 - 0.05).
%[text] The power of the pump moving water between the cooling tower and chiller unit is given by:
%[text]  $P\_{\\mathrm{Pump}} =\\frac{\\dot{m} \\times g\\times H}{{\\eta \\times \\rho }\_{\\mathrm{Water}} }${"editStyle":"visual"}, where H is the nominal pump head, $\\eta${"editStyle":"visual"} the pump efficiency, $\\rho${"editStyle":"visual"} is water density.
%[text] The chiller condenser water flow rate $\\dot{m}${"editStyle":"visual"} is calculated from the energy balance equation:
%[text]  $\\dot{m} \\times C\_{P,\\mathrm{water}} \\times \\bigtriangleup T\_{\\mathrm{CT}} =Q\_{\\mathrm{CT}} \\;${"editStyle":"visual"}, where $\\bigtriangleup T\_{\\mathrm{CT}}${"editStyle":"visual"} denotes the cooling tower (temperature) range, in degC.
%[text]  $\\bigtriangleup T\_{\\mathrm{CT}} =T\_{\\mathrm{Hot}} \\sim T\_{\\mathrm{Cold}}${"editStyle":"visual"}
%[text] These equations for the chiller and cooling tower are implemented in the **Chiller** and **Cooling Tower** subsystems, respectively. On the Chiller block, the *Pc* and *Ton* ports output the chiller power requirement in watts and the tonnage. On the **Cooling Tower** block, the *Pp* and *Pf* ports output the power consumption at the cooling tower water pump and the cooling tower fan, respectively.
%[text] The **HVAC (Room)** subsystem estimates the energy required to cool the room air to the desired set-point temperature. The *P* port outputs the electrical power consumption of the HVAC subsystem.
%[text] Specify chiller COP and HVAC heat exchanger and cooling tower pump efficiency.
modelData.ControlParam.Chiller.COP = 4;
modelData.ControlParam.PercentEff.HVAC = 78;
modelData.ControlParam.PercentEff.PUMP = 80;
%[text] Specify cooling tower parameters.
modelData.ControlParam.CoolingTower.Trange = simscape.Value(8,"K");
modelData.ControlParam.CoolingTower.TowerFanPowerRatio = 0.02;
%[text] ### Set Geographical Location for Analysis
%[text] Specify location.
modelData.LocationName    = "London";
modelData.Location        = getGeoLocationForMajorCities(CityName=modelData.LocationName);
modelData.Place.Latitude  = getGeographicalCoordinates(modelData.Location.Latitude);
modelData.Place.Longitude = getGeographicalCoordinates(modelData.Location.Longitude);
modelData.Place.Meredian  = getGeographicalCoordinates(modelData.Location.("Meredian (Time Zone)"));
%[text] ### Specify Seasonal Temperature Variation
%[text] Specify the monthly minimum and maximum temperatures recorded at the specified geographical location. This data is used to estimate the daily temperature variation using the `getTemperatureFromYearlyData` function. If daily temperature variation data is already available, skip this step and define the `modelData.AvgDayT`, `modelData.AvgDayTvar`, `modelData.AvgNightT`, and `modelData.AvgNightTvar` parameters directly (see below).
modelData.YearTavg = simscape.Value([272,276; 272 278; 275 283; ... % Q1 months (min,max)
                                     278 287; 282 292; 286 295; ... % Q2 months (min,max)
                                     287 297; 284 292; 280 287; ... % Q3 months (min,max)
                                     276 281; 276 281; 272 277],... % Q4 months (min,max)
                                     "K");
%[text] Convert yearly data for temperature into day-wise variation.
[modelData.AvgDayT,modelData.AvgDayTvar,...  %[output:group:46f10be0] %[output:22222d6c]
 modelData.AvgNightT,modelData.AvgNightTvar] = ... %[output:22222d6c]
            getTemperatureFromYearlyData(...  %[output:22222d6c]
                              DateTimeVec=modelData.DateTimeVec,... %[output:22222d6c]
                              Tavg12MonthData=modelData.YearTavg,... %[output:22222d6c]
                              DeltaDegreesNightT=simscape.Value(ceil(value(sum(diff(modelData.YearTavg'))/length(diff(modelData.YearTavg')),"K")),"K"),...  %[output:22222d6c]
                              Plot=true,... %[output:22222d6c]
                              PlotName=modelData.LocationName,... %[output:22222d6c]
                              Location=modelData.Location,...  %[output:22222d6c]
                              PercentDayTimeTvar=2,... %[output:22222d6c]
                              PercentNightTimeTvar=3);  %[output:group:46f10be0] %[output:22222d6c]
%%
%[text] ## Run Simulation
%[text] %[text:anchor:TMP_5ae1] Open the model for analysis.
modelData.SLXModelName = "SizeDataCenterCoolingSystem";
open_system(modelData.SLXModelName);
%[text] Set total run time for simulation.
set_param(modelData.SLXModelName, 'StopTime', strcat(num2str((length(hour(modelData.DateTimeVec))-1)*3600),"% hours ~ ",num2str(length(hour(modelData.DateTimeVec))-1)));
%[text] Setup HVAC operation for room.
modelData.ControlParam.HVACswitch = 1; % 1 is ON, 0 is OFF
%[text] Apply design parameters (specifed above, `modelData`) to the model.
setDesignParameters(modelData.SLXModelName,modelData.ControlParam,string(datetime("now")));
%[text] ### Setup PUE Calculation
%[text] The PUE value for the system is defined through the output port *PUE,* on the **Sensor** subsytem. The *PUE* value is defined as $PUE=\\frac{\\mathrm{Total}\\;\\mathrm{Facility}\\;\\mathrm{Energy}}{\\mathrm{IT}\\;\\mathrm{Equipment}\\;\\mathrm{Energy}}=\\frac{E\_{\\mathrm{P}\\mathrm{D}\\mathrm{U}} +E\_{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{D}\\mathrm{U}} +E\_{\\mathrm{C}\\mathrm{H}\\mathrm{I}\\mathrm{L}\\mathrm{L}\\mathrm{E}\\mathrm{R}} +E\_{\\mathrm{H}\\mathrm{V}\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{C}} +E\_{\\mathrm{F}\\mathrm{A}\\mathrm{N}} +E\_{\\mathrm{P}\\mathrm{U}\\mathrm{M}\\mathrm{P}} }{E\_{\\mathrm{P}\\mathrm{D}\\mathrm{U}} }${"editStyle":"visual"}.
%[text] ### Simulate Model
%[text] Run model and close.
simRes = sim(modelData.SLXModelName);
close_system(modelData.SLXModelName,1);
%%
%[text] ## Analyze Results
%[text] Extract results.
simResTbl = logsout_SizeDataCenterCoolingSystem.extractTimetable;
simResTbl = simResTbl(timerange(hours(24),hours(length(modelData.DateTimeVec))),:);
%[text] Calculate weekly average data.
simResTblWeek = retime(simResTbl, "regular", "mean", "TimeStep", days(7));
%[text] Plot power consumption for different components.
bar(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), [simResTblWeek.("Power (W).PDU"),... %[output:11151e67]
                                   simResTblWeek.("Power (W).CDU"),... %[output:11151e67]
                                   simResTblWeek.("Power (W).Room_HVAC"),... %[output:11151e67]
                                   simResTblWeek.("Power (W).Chiller"),... %[output:11151e67]
                                   simResTblWeek.("Power (W).Condenser_Pump"),... %[output:11151e67]
                                   simResTblWeek.("Power (W).Cooling_Tower_Fan")]/1000,"stacked"); %[output:11151e67]
xlabel("# Week"); ylabel("Power (kW)"); %[output:11151e67]
legend(["PDU","CDU","Room HVAC","Chiller","Cooling Tower Pump","Cooling Tower Fan"],Location="eastoutside"); %[output:11151e67]
title("Power Consumption"); %[output:11151e67]
%[text] Plot weekly Power Usage Effectiveness, or the PUE, variation.
figure("Name","PUE"); %[output:8276788a]
plot(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), simResTblWeek.PUE,"-o"); %[output:8276788a]
xlabel("# Week"); ylabel("PUE (-)"); %[output:8276788a]
title("PUE = Total Facility Energy / IT Equipment Energy"); %[output:8276788a]
%[text] Plot weekly chiller power requirement.
figure("Name","Chiller"); %[output:3691ec11]
plot(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), simResTblWeek.("Capacity (Chiller Tonnage)"),"-o"); %[output:3691ec11]
xlabel("# Week"); ylabel("Tonnage"); %[output:3691ec11]
title("Chiller Power"); %[output:3691ec11]
%[text] Plot weekly HVAC power requirement.
figure("Name","HVAC"); %[output:0af7fcd2]
plot(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), simResTblWeek.("Capacity (HVAC kW)"),"-o"); %[output:0af7fcd2]
xlabel("# Week"); ylabel("HVAC kW"); %[output:0af7fcd2]
title("HVAC Power"); %[output:0af7fcd2]
%[text] Plot weekly cooling tower power consumption.
figure("Name","Cooling Tower"); %[output:82a42646]
plot(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), (simResTblWeek.("Power (W).Condenser_Pump")+simResTblWeek.("Power (W).Cooling_Tower_Fan"))/1000,"-o"); %[output:82a42646]
xlabel("# Week"); ylabel("Cooling Tower kW"); %[output:82a42646]
title("Cooling Tower Pump + Fan Power"); %[output:82a42646]
%[text] Plot temperatures.
figure("Name","Temperature"); %[output:38150ae3]
plot(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), simResTblWeek.("T (K).server"),"-o"); hold on; %[output:38150ae3]
plot(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), simResTblWeek.("T (K).room"),"-*"); hold on; %[output:38150ae3]
plot(1:length(simResTblWeek.Time), simResTblWeek.("T (K).ambient"),"-+"); hold off; %[output:38150ae3]
legend("Server","Room","Ambient",Location="eastoutside"); %[output:38150ae3]
xlabel("# Week"); ylabel("Temperature (K)"); %[output:38150ae3]
title("Temperature Profile"); %[output:38150ae3]
%%
%[text] Display cooling component rating required for the data center system.
modelData.ComponentRating = getResultSummaryTbl(simResTblWeek); %[output:5aae1181]

